\sigma(\mathcal{W}^{(0)},(X_{i}^{\prime},A_{i},R_{i})_{i\in[m]})=\sigma(\mathcal{W}^{(0)},\mathcal{D}_{m})=\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{tr}}.# Appendix D From Logged Data to Arm-wise State EvolutionThis section reduces the logged bandit data to the setting of 1.1.1/2.1.1/1.1.18. Conditional on the action labels and counts, each arm gives a Gaussian single-index regression problem with its own initialization and noise vector. We then append the target-policy index to the auxiliary GFOM iterates. This allows the state-evolution test functions to include the importance weights.## D.1 Arm-wise conditioning and admissibilityFor $0<c_{-}<c_{+}<\infty$, let@equation
