Under the relabeling $m=N_{a}$, $n=d$, $\mu_{\ast}=\beta_{a}$, and $\bm{\varphi}=\varphi_{a,[q]}^{\ast}$, HI25 Assumption (A1) follows on $E_{\mathrm{cnt}}$ from $N_{a}/d\in[c_{-},c_{+}]$, and (A2) follows from the Gaussian design. Assumptions (A3)–(A4) are precisely the learning-rate and activation conditions in Assumption 1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.35, and (A5) with coordinate-specific reward links follows from the same assumption and 1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.66. The initialization is independent of the design by assumption. Comparing (1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.46) with HI25 () gives the stated identity for $\varkappa_{\ast,a}$. Thus, the relabeled arm-wise problem satisfies the hypotheses of the HI25 comparison results as extended in 1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.66.


