0_{(L-1)q\times\ell}\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{L,q}\times\ell},so that $A_{a}\Upsilon_{\mathrm{pad},a}=X_{a}\Upsilon$. Let $(u_{a}^{(t)},v_{a}^{(t)})$ denote the auxiliary GFOM iterates in HI25, Section 7.2 and HI25 Proposition, using the padded reward link $\varphi_{a,[q]}^{\ast}$. The matrix $u_{a}^{(t)}$ has one row per observation, whereas $v_{a}^{(t)}$ has one row per input coordinate or padded parameter coordinate. We refer to the corresponding state-evolution descriptions as row-indexed and column-indexed, respectively. Define the iterates with appended target-policy index coordinates by@equation
