By (1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.27), on $\mathcal{A}_{b}$ the actual deeper trajectory lies in the ball of radius $R=(C_{b}\kappa\log n)^{C_{T}}$. Choose a deterministic $\delta$-net of this ball, with $\delta=(C_{b}n\kappa R\log n)^{-C_{T}-1}$, so that every trajectory is within $\delta$ of a net point. The net can be chosen with cardinality at most


