Apply (1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.31) at each net point with its tail exponent larger than $b_{0}+C_{T}+2$, and take a union bound over the net. By (1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.34), replacing any trajectory by its nearest net point changes each hidden state by at most one. Thus, the bound extends to the whole ball, with failure probability at most $(C_{b_{0}}\kappa\log n)^{C_{b_{0}}}n^{-b_{0}}$. For the random choice $B^{(s)}=W_{[2:L]}^{(s)}$, induction in (1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.30) gives $v_{B}^{(s)}=\sqrt{n}W_{1}^{(s)}$ exactly. No independence between this random path and $A$ is needed after the simultaneous bound has been established. This proves (1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.17).


