Proof.
Throughout, we fix an arm $a$ and suppress the subscript $a$, retaining $\phi_{a}$ for the arm-wise sample-to-dimension ratio. To match HI25 within this proof, use $m$ for the arm-wise sample size $N_{a}$, rather than the full logged sample size, and set $n=d$. Write $X\coloneqq X_{a}$, $\phi_{a}=m/n=N_{a}/d$, and $\beta\coloneqq\beta_{a}$. Retain the definitions above and set $n_{L,q}\coloneqq d_{L,q}$, $A\coloneqq A_{a}$, $\Upsilon_{\mathrm{pad}}\coloneqq\Upsilon_{\mathrm{pad},a}$, and $\bar{\mu}_{\ast,n}\coloneqq\bar{\mu}_{a,\ast,d}$. Thus, $A\Upsilon_{\mathrm{pad}}=X\Upsilon$. Under $\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}[\cdot]$, before appending the target-policy index, the arm-wise padded problem is covered by 1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.66 under the relabeling $m=N_{a}$, $n=d$, $\mu_{\ast}=\beta_{a}$, and $\bm{\varphi}=\varphi_{a,[q]}^{\ast}$. Let $(u^{(t)},v^{(t)})$ denote the corresponding auxiliary GFOM iterates, and let $\Theta_{k}^{(s)}$ and $V_{\alpha}^{(s)}$ be the original arm-wise state evolution objects from HI25 Proposition.


