The new blocks follow directly from


$$\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}[Q_{j}^{(s)}]^{\top}\sqrt{n}\,\Upsilon_{j\cdot}$$


Thus, the index–index covariance equals $I_{\ell}$ for every pair of times. If $J^{(s)}$ and $J^{(r)}$ are two such Gaussian index states, then


1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.133


Thus, the index states share the same Gaussian vector at every time.


For the appended index coordinates, the row-indexed iterate equals the rowwise linear feature $X\Upsilon$ at every time. Denote the common Gaussian index vector by $\mathfrak{U}_{\Upsilon}$. Since $\Upsilon^{\top}\Upsilon=I_{\ell}$ and $X_{k\cdot}^{\top}\sim N(0,I_{n})$ under $\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}$, this vector has law $N(0,I_{\ell})$. Let


