The deeper auxiliary blocks satisfy $(\widetilde{v}_{\alpha}^{(s)})^{\mathrm{aux}}=v_{\alpha}^{(s)}=V_{\alpha}^{(s)}$ exactly, because the padded columns of $A$ vanish. This proves item 1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.115.


For delocalization, put $B_{t}=C_{t}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t}}$. The rowwise bound in HI25 Proposition, with its tail parameter chosen as $C\log d$, gives after increasing $C_{t}$


$$\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{a}^{(0)}\left(\|u^{(t)}\|_{\infty}\vee\|v^{(t)}\|_{\infty}>B_{t}\right)$$


because $N_{a}+n_{L,q}=O(d)$ on $E_{\mathrm{cnt}}$ and $q$ is fixed. The appended coordinates are explicit:


1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.148


Each entry of $X\Upsilon$ is $N(0,1)$. Hence, for every $z>0$,


1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.149


Taking $z=C\sqrt{\log d}$ and increasing $C$ makes this probability at most $d^{-101}$. Since $\varkappa_{\ast,a}\geq 1$, this threshold is bounded by $B_{t}$ after increasing $C_{t}$. A union bound proves item 1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.117.
