Proof.
After the relabeling $m=N_{a}$, $n=d$, and $\mu_{\ast}=\beta_{a}$, 1.1.1/1.1.10/1.2.9 verifies the assumptions for the arm-wise problem with $\bm{\varphi}=\varphi_{a,[q]}^{\ast}$. The parameter and Onsager-coefficient comparisons follow from 1.1.1/1.1.10/1.3.83, applied at horizon $t+1$. We derive the corrected-state comparisons from those estimates and the deterministic loss-gradient bounds. For the first difference, the definitions give


