kind: definition (Definition E.2 (Test functions for weighted averages).)
Fix $a\in[K]$ and $t\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$. A family of functions $\Phi_{t,k}:\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}^{q}\times\mathbb{R}^{\ell}\to\mathbb{R}$, $k\in[N]$, satisfies the comparison conditions if it is measurable with respect to $\sigma(\mathcal{I}_{a},\xi_{[N]},W_{a}^{(0)})$ and, conditional on $\mathcal{G}_{a}$, there are a fixed integer $p\geq 1$ and $L_{a,t}\leq C_{t}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t}}$ such that, for every $k\in[N]$, $z,z^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}$, $w\in\mathbb{R}^{q}$, and $s\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell}$,


$$\displaystyle|\Phi_{t,k}(z,w,s)-\Phi_{t,k}(z^{\prime},w,s)|$$


Moreover, with


1.1.1/1.1.11/1.3.5


the family $\{\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}\}_{k=1}^{N}$ satisfies the following pseudo-Lipschitz and origin bounds with the same $p$ and $L_{a,t}$:


$$\displaystyle|\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}(x)-\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}(x^{\prime})|$$@equation
\displaystyle|\Phi_{t,k}(z,w,s)-\Phi_{t,k}(z^{\prime},w,s)|@equation
\displaystyle|\Phi_{t,k}(0,w,s)|@equation
\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}(u,w,s)\coloneqq\Phi_{t,k}\bigl(G_{V^{(t)}}(u),w,s\bigr),@equation
\displaystyle|\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}(x)-\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}(x^{\prime})|@equation
\displaystyle|\Theta_{\Phi,t,k}(0)|The first bound allows the Lipschitz factor to grow at most linearly in the scalar prediction. This lets us compare empirical averages using the normalized $\ell_{2}$ bounds for the corrected states. The composed state-evolution test function may have any fixed pseudo-Lipschitz order. For each family satisfying these conditions, the constants below depend only on that order and the fixed constants in the displayed bounds; they are uniform in $d$ and the row index $k$.For such a family, we compare the corrected empirical average with the expectation of the same test at an independent context. With $Z\sim N(0,I_{d})$ independent of $\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{tr}}$ and of $\pi_{N}$, define these two quantities and the state-evolution expectation used to compare them by@equation
\displaystyle\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{a}^{(t)}(\Phi)@equation
\displaystyle\mathcal{O}_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)@equation
\displaystyle\Gamma_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)@theorem
kind: suppproposition (Proposition S.3 (Comparison with expectations at independent contexts).)
Assume the conditions of 1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.1. Fix $a\in[K]$, $t\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$, and a family satisfying 1.1.1/1.1.11/1.3.2. For every $r\geq 1$, there is a constant $C_{t,r}<\infty$, depending only on the fixed pseudo-Lipschitz order and the constants in that definition, such that, on $E_{\mathrm{cnt}}$,


$$\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}|\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{a}^{(t)}(\Phi)-\Gamma_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)|^{r}+\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}|\mathcal{O}_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)-\Gamma_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)|^{r}\leq C_{t,r}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t,r}}d^{-1/C_{t,r}}.$$


Consequently,


1.1.1/1.1.11/1.3.15@equation
\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}|\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{a}^{(t)}(\Phi)-\Gamma_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)|^{r}+\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}|\mathcal{O}_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)-\Gamma_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)|^{r}\leq C_{t,r}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t,r}}d^{-1/C_{t,r}}.@equation
\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}|\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{a}^{(t)}(\Phi)-\mathcal{O}_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)|^{r}\leq C_{t,r}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t,r}}d^{-1/C_{t,r}}.@proof
Proof.
We first compare $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{a}^{(t)}(\Phi)$ with the state-evolution average $\Gamma_{a,\pi}^{(t)}(\Phi)$. We replace the deeper-layer weights and corrected states in stages, using 1.1.1/1.1.11/1.2.36. Define the resulting prediction vectors by


$$\displaystyle z_{k}^{(0)}$$


For $j=0,\ldots,4$, put


