\mathbb{E}_{a}^{(0)}|\widehat{M}_{a,\mathrm{diag}}^{(t)}-M_{a}^{(t)}|^{r}\leq C_{t,r}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t,r}}d^{-1/C_{t,r}}.@equation
\sup_{t\in\mathcal{T}}|\widehat{M}_{a,\mathrm{diag}}^{(t)}-M_{a}^{(t)}|\xrightarrow{p}0.@proof
Proof.
Take $\Phi_{t,k}^{\mathrm{fit}}(z,w,s)\coloneqq h(s)z$. Boundedness and Lipschitz continuity of $h$, together with HI25 Proposition -(1)(2), verify the conditions in 1.1.1/1.1.11/1.3.2. The two quantities in 1.1.1/1.1.11/1.3.13 are


1.1.1/1.1.12/1.4.10


Because $W_{a}^{(t)}$ is $\widehat{\mathcal{F}}_{a}$-measurable and $Z$ is independent of both conditioning fields,


$$\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[w_{a}(Z)f_{W_{a}^{(t)}}(Z)\,|\,\widehat{\mathcal{F}}_{a}\right]$$


1.1.1/1.1.11/1.3.13 therefore gives the conditional moment bound. For fixed $\epsilon>0$ and $r\geq 1$, conditional Markov’s inequality yields


$$\displaystyle\mathbb{P}\left(\sup_{t\in\mathcal{T}}|\widehat{M}_{a,\mathrm{diag}}^{(t)}-M_{a}^{(t)}|>\epsilon\right)\leq\mathbb{P}(E_{\mathrm{cnt}}^{c})+\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{1}_{E_{\mathrm{cnt}}}\min\left\{1,\epsilon^{-r}C_{t,r}(\varkappa_{\ast,a}\log d)^{C_{t,r}}d^{-1/C_{t,r}}\right\}\right].$$




Each integrand in the sum is bounded by one and converges in probability to zero by (1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.50); hence, its expectation converges to zero. Since $\mathbb{P}(E_{\mathrm{cnt}}^{c})\to 0$, this proves (1.1.1/1.1.12/1.4.8).
