\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\nu}(\tilde{g})@equation
\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[w_{A}(X)\varepsilon\delta_{\tilde{g}}(X,A)\,|\,\mathcal{H}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[w_{A}(X)\delta_{\tilde{g}}(X,A)\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon\,|\,X,A,\mathcal{H}]\,|\,\mathcal{H}\right]=0.These finite-sample conclusions use only the logging probabilities and the conditional mean of the reward; they do not require the neural-network assumptions.## G.3 Proof of Theorem 4.2See 1.1.1/1.1.4/1.2.8@proof
