kind: remark (Remark H.5.)
The predictors in 1.1.1/1.1.14/1.2.13 are represented by the permitted network with depth two, width one, and identity activation: take $W_{1}=\theta$ and $W_{2}=1$. The architecture and scaling assumptions therefore do not imply local stochastic equicontinuity over the entire predictor class.We now analyze the DR estimator formed from the fitted gradient-descent iterates. Order the arm-$a$ observations as $\mathcal{I}_{a}=\{i_{a,1},\ldots,i_{a,N_{a}}\}$, and define the weighted average of the uncorrected predictions on that arm’s training observations by@equation
\widetilde{M}_{a,\mathrm{diag}}^{(t)}\coloneqq\frac{1}{N_{a}}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{a}}w_{a}(X_{i})G_{W_{a,[2:L]}^{(t)}}(X_{i}^{\top}W_{a,1}^{(t)}).Write $V_{a}^{(t)}\coloneqq(V_{a,\alpha}^{(t)})_{\alpha\in[2:L]}$ for the deeper-layer quantities in the state evolution, and define the state-evolution approximation to this training-sample average by@equation
