In the nonparametric model with known logging probabilities and unrestricted context and reward distributions, $\psi_{g^{\ast}}-\mathcal{V}(\nu)$ is the efficient influence function [1.1.1/2.1.1/1.1.24]. The Gaussian single-index model considered here imposes additional restrictions, so its efficiency bound requires a separate calculation. The notation $\sigma_{\mathrm{eff}}^{2}$ in 1.1.1/1.1.4/1.3.26 denotes the variance of $\psi_{g^{\ast}}$.


The state-evolution results in this paper assume that the arm-wise aspect ratios stay bounded above and away from zero, with fixed network width and training horizon. Extending these results to $m/d\to\infty$, growing width, or a growing training horizon requires new bounds that are uniform in the corresponding parameters.@equation
\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{or}}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\psi_{g^{\ast}}(Q_{i}).@equation
\sqrt{m}\{\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{ADR}}(\mathbf{t})-\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{or}}\}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{m}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\left[\sum_{a=1}^{K}\nu(a\mid X_{i})\Delta_{i,a}-w_{A_{i}}(X_{i})\Delta_{i,A_{i}}\right].@equation
\sqrt{m}\{\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{ADR}}(\widehat{\mathbf{t}})-\mathcal{V}(\nu)\}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{m}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\{\psi_{g^{\ast}}(Q_{i})-\mathcal{V}(\nu)\}+o_{p}(1),@equation
\sqrt{m}\{\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{ADR}}(\widehat{\mathbf{t}})-\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{or}}\}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{m}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}H_{g_{\widehat{\mathbf{t}}},d}(Q_{i}^{\prime})=o_{p}(1),@equation
S_{m}^{\prime}\coloneqq\frac{1}{\sqrt{m}}\sum_{i=1}^{m}H_{g_{\widehat{\mathbf{t}}},d}(Q_{i}^{\prime}).@equation
