\displaystyle=\mathcal{J}_{\mathrm{var}}(g_{\widehat{\mathbf{t}}}).@equation
\mathbb{P}(|S_{m}^{\prime}|>\epsilon)\leq\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left\{1,\epsilon^{-2}\mathcal{J}_{\mathrm{var}}(g_{\widehat{\mathbf{t}}})\right\}\right]\longrightarrow 0@equation
\min_{\mathbf{t}\in\mathcal{T}^{K}}\mathcal{R}_{\nu}^{\circ}(g_{\mathbf{t}})=o_{p}(1).## H.2 Variance of the DR score on an independent observationWe evaluate $\psi_{g}(X,A,R)$ on an observation independent of the sample used to fit $g$. Conditional on $\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{tr}}$, this score has mean $\mathcal{V}(\nu)$ under the known logging policy. The next proposition decomposes its conditional variance and bounds the part that depends on $g$ by the target-policy-weighted prediction risk. To obtain the sampling variance of ADR, one must also account for covariances between the adjusted terms evaluated on different training observations.For an independent observation $(X,A,R)$ and a reward model $g$, define@equation
