c_{-}(\mu)\coloneqq\min_{a\in[K]}\frac{1-\mu(a)}{\mu(a)},\qquad c_{+}(\mu)\coloneqq\max_{a\in[K]}\frac{1-\mu(a)}{\mu(a)}.@theorem
kind: proposition (Proposition H.10 (Excess variance of the DR score).)
Assume $K\geq 2$, known context-independent logging with $\mu(a)>0$ for every arm, and rewards $R=g^{\ast}(X,A)+\varepsilon$ whose noise law satisfies (1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.41). Suppose $\mathbb{E}[R^{2}]<\infty$. Let $g$ be a deterministic measurable reward model or an $\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{tr}}$-measurable fitted reward model, with $\mathcal{R}_{\nu}^{\circ}(g)<\infty$ almost surely. Let $(X,A,R)$ follow the logged-data law independently of $\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{tr}}$. Then, almost surely,


$$\displaystyle\operatorname{Var}(\psi_{g}\,|\,X,\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{tr}})$$


Moreover,


