\max_{a\in[K]}\mathbb{E}\left[\varkappa_{\ast,a}^{s}\right]\leq C_{s}(\log d)^{C_{s}}\qquad\text{for each fixed }s\geq 1.Because $\varkappa_{\ast,a}$ contains $\|\xi_{\mathcal{I}_{a}}\|_{\infty}$, this condition is stronger than the envelope assumption used above. It provides the polylogarithmic second- and fourth-moment bounds for the triangular-array noise laws used below.@theorem
kind: proposition (Proposition I.1 (Polynomial rates under the strengthened envelope).)
Assume the conditions of Section 1.1.1/1.1.9/1.1.1 and (1.1.1/1.1.15/1.1.3), with fixed $K,L,q,\mathcal{T}$. There exists $\beta_{HI25}>0$, independent of $d$, such that, for every $0<\beta<\beta_{0}\coloneqq\min\{\beta_{HI25},1/2\}$, as $d\to\infty$, the corrected risk criterion satisfies


$$\displaystyle\max_{a\in[K]}\sup_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left\lvert\widehat{\mathcal{E}}_{a}^{(t)}-\mathcal{E}_{a,\mathrm{ind}}^{(t)}\right\rvert$$


and the value estimators satisfy


$$\displaystyle\sup_{\mathbf{t}\in\mathcal{T}^{K}}\left\lvert\widehat{\mathcal{V}}_{\mathrm{ADM}}(\mathbf{t})-\mathcal{V}_{g_{\mathbf{t}}}(\nu)\right\rvert$$@equation
