venue: pp. 3589–3597
text: Y. Wang, A. Agarwal, and M. Dudík Optimal and adaptive off-policy evaluation in contextual bandits. In International Conference on Machine Learning, pp. 3589–3597.@figure
kind: algorithm
caption: Full-sample model selection and adjusted policy evaluation
1:


 Logged sample $\mathcal{D}_{m}$, known $\mu$, fixed target policy $\nu$, initializations, learning-rate schedules, and fixed iterate grid $\mathcal{T}$.
2:


 for each arm $a\in[K]$ do
3:


   Train all layers by full-batch GD on $\mathcal{L}_{a}$ through $T=\max\mathcal{T}$.
4:


   Compute $\widehat{\rho}_{a,t,s}$ by Appendix 1.1.1/1.1.8/1.1.1 and $\widehat{U}_{i,a}^{(t)}$ by (1.1.1/1.1.3/1.2.7).
5:


   Evaluate $\widehat{\mathcal{E}}_{a}^{(t)}$ for $t\in\mathcal{T}$ and select $\hat{t}_{a}$ by (1.1.1/1.1.3/1.3.7).
6:


 end for
7:


 Form the adjusted training predictions (1.1.1/1.1.3/1.3.11) at $\widehat{\mathbf{t}}$.
8:


 Compute ADM and ADR by (1.1.1/1.1.3/1.3.13) and (1.1.1/1.1.3/1.3.15).
9:


 return $g_{\widehat{\mathbf{t}}}$ for new-context prediction, and the two adjusted value estimates.@figure
kind: figure
source: proportional_growth_risk_selection.svg
