caption: Risk estimation and stopping-time selection with $m=2d$ and 200 datasets per dimension. Left: RMSE in estimating the full-data models’ conditional arm-wise test risks, with squared errors averaged over arms, candidate iterations, and datasets. Right: mean total target-policy prediction-risk regret of the selected full-data model, on a logarithmic scale. Bars give pointwise $95\%$ Monte Carlo intervals.<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" version="1.1" width="492.68376pt" height="199.69063pt" viewBox="0 0 492.68376 199.69063">
