caption: Effect of target-policy weighting on stopping decisions for identical full-data trajectories. Points show the mean paired difference across datasets in selection regret between the corrected weighted criterion and the corrected unweighted criterion (left) or target-weighted ten-fold CV (right). Negative values favor the corrected weighted criterion. Bars give pointwise $95\%$ Monte Carlo intervals over 200 datasets per dimension. All four target policies are shown.<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" version="1.1" width="485.23188pt" height="199.69063pt" viewBox="0 0 485.23188 199.69063">
