caption: Risk estimation, stopping-time selection, and value bias under
context-independent logging, with $\mu(2)=1-\mu(1)$, $m=2d$, and 200 datasets per setting. Top: root mean squared error in estimating the full-data models’ total target-policy test risk, with squared errors averaged over all pairs of stopping times and datasets. Middle: mean total prediction-risk regret of the selected full-data models. These two rows use logarithmic vertical axes. Bottom: empirical bias of DR and ADR at identical models and stopping times selected by the corrected criterion. Bars give pointwise $95\%$ Monte Carlo intervals across datasets.<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" version="1.1" width="567.1413pt" height="508.4936pt" viewBox="0 0 567.1413 508.4936">
