caption: Risk estimation and value estimation under three context
distributions, with $m=2d$ and 200 datasets per setting. Top: root mean squared error in estimating the full-data models’ conditional arm-wise test risks, with squared errors averaged over both arms, all candidate iterations, and datasets. These risks include reward noise and use $w_{a}(X)=2\nu(a\mid X)$; the vertical axis is logarithmic. Bottom: empirical bias of DR and ADR relative to the true policy value, at identical models and stopping times selected by the corrected criterion. Bars give pointwise $95\%$ Monte Carlo intervals across datasets.<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" version="1.1" width="391.46763pt" height="283.35877pt" viewBox="0 0 391.46763 283.35877">
