</svg>@figure
kind: table
caption: Stopping-time selection under three context distributions,
with $m=2d$ and 200 datasets per setting. Regret is measured by the total target-policy prediction risk $\mathcal{R}_{\nu}^{\circ}$ relative to the best pair of stopping times on the full-data trajectories. Parentheses give Monte Carlo standard errors. The last two columns report the paired regret difference between the corrected rule and ten-fold cross-validation, with pointwise $95\%$ Monte Carlo intervals.
Context law | $d$ | Corrected regret | Corrected minus CV | $95\%$ interval
Gaussian | $256$ | $0.0141$ $(0.0020)$ | $-0.0045$ | $[-0.0082,\,-0.0008]$
 | $1024$ | $0.0043$ $(0.0007)$ | $-0.0050$ | $[-0.0070,\,-0.0031]$
 | $2048$ | $0.0025$ $(0.0005)$ | $-0.0057$ | $[-0.0076,\,-0.0038]$
Rademacher | $256$ | $0.0138$ $(0.0018)$ | $-0.0066$ | $[-0.0106,\,-0.0025]$
 | $1024$ | $0.0054$ $(0.0007)$ | $-0.0063$ | $[-0.0086,\,-0.0041]$
 | $2048$ | $0.0042$ $(0.0006)$ | $-0.0059$ | $[-0.0077,\,-0.0041]$
Standardized $t_{5}$ | $256$ | $0.0154$ $(0.0018)$ | $-0.0089$ | $[-0.0127,\,-0.0050]$
 | $1024$ | $0.0066$ $(0.0009)$ | $-0.0041$ | $[-0.0062,\,-0.0020]$
 | $2048$ | $0.0027$ $(0.0005)$ | $-0.0059$ | $[-0.0077,\,-0.0040]$@figure
kind: table
caption: Median runtime in seconds for complete selection and value
estimation on an Intel Xeon E5-2680 v3. Both CF10 procedures exclude each evaluation fold from fitting and selection. CV includes full-data refitting and raw DR scoring.
$d$ | $m$ | ADR | Ten-fold CV
+ refit | CF10
(inner validation) | CF10
(corrected stopping)
$512$ | $1024$ | $2.55$ | $1.44$ | $1.34$ | $13.97$
$2048$ | $4096$ | $8.15$ | $16.68$ | $13.26$ | $66.74$
$1024$ | $32768$ | $51.84$ | $86.02$ | $133.29$ | $462.31$@figure
kind: table
caption: Median runtime in seconds in a separate matched holdout study on
an Intel Xeon Gold 6230R. All procedures include selection and final scoring; CV and holdouts also include full-data refitting.
